  "schema": "trillion.file-previews",
  "about": "What each file on the Files screen shows as its picture. A stored media type's matching prefix takes precedence over the name's extension for ambiguous sound and video containers; otherwise `families_by_extension` names its family. A file whose extension is not listed is `other`. A file's content type is the one it was stored with, else `content_types_by_extension`; the one file preview picks its viewer from it, else from the extension (parts/ui/show/file-preview/file-viewers.json). `made: true` means the browser makes the file's small pictures (a picture's still, or the preview a camera's raw photo carries inside it; a video's still and a strip of frames to scrub; a sound's waveform; a PDF's first page; a written file's opening lines) once and keeps them with the file (parts/ui/show/media-preview/made-preview.tsx). Rows are read in order and the first row whose `family` matches wins; a row without `family` matches every file. `renderer` names a shared MediaPreview renderer (parts/ui/show/media-preview); `moment_renderer`, when set, is the renderer for one moment inside the file (a search result, a found moment: a video's frame at that second); `picture: true` shows the file's own bytes as its picture; `icon` and `type_label` name its fallback picture and kind. New ambiguous media kinds are DATA rows here. `tree_tone`, when set, is the tone of the shared look the file's icon is drawn in wherever it shows in the folder tree.",
